---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
import CodeBlock from "../../components/CodeBlock.astro";
import {
  FILE_STRUCTURE,
  REPRO_MD_CONTENT,
  TRACE_EXCERPT,
  ASSERTION_TYPES,
} from "../../content/snippets";
---

<Base title="Specification — repro.md" description="The repro.md format specification — trace events, assertions, blob storage, and the REPRO.md manifest.">

  <section style="padding-top: var(--space-2xl);">
    <div class="container container--narrow">
      <p class="section-label">Specification</p>
      <h1 style="font-size: clamp(1.75rem, 4vw, 2.25rem);">repro.md format</h1>
      <p class="subtitle">The reproduction artifact format for AI agent failures.</p>
      <p class="prose" style="margin-top: var(--space-md);">Version 0.1</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Overview -->
  <section>
    <div class="container container--narrow">
      <h2 id="overview">Overview</h2>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>A repro artifact is a directory containing a recorded trace of an AI agent run, plus optional assertions. The trace captures every model API request and response, allowing the run to be replayed deterministically without an API key.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Directory structure -->
  <section>
    <div class="container container--narrow">
      <h2 id="structure">Directory structure</h2>
      <CodeBlock filename=".repro/" id="spec-structure" code={FILE_STRUCTURE} />
      <div class="prose">
        <p>Each recording gets a unique directory under <code>.repro/</code>. IDs are prefixed with <code>r-</code> followed by a short hex identifier.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Trace format -->
  <section>
    <div class="container container--narrow">
      <h2 id="trace">Trace format</h2>
      <div class="prose">
        <p><code>trace.json</code> is a JSON array of events. Each event has a sequence number, type, timestamp, and data payload.</p>
      </div>

      <CodeBlock filename="trace.json" lang="json" id="spec-trace" code={TRACE_EXCERPT} />

      <h3 id="event-types" style="margin-top: var(--space-xl);">Event types</h3>
      <div class="assertion-list" style="margin-top: var(--space-md);">
        <div class="assertion">
          <span class="assertion-type">process.start</span>
          <span class="assertion-desc">Agent process started. Data: command, pid.</span>
        </div>
        <div class="assertion">
          <span class="assertion-type">process.exit</span>
          <span class="assertion-desc">Agent process exited. Data: exit code.</span>
        </div>
        <div class="assertion">
          <span class="assertion-type">model.request</span>
          <span class="assertion-desc">Model API request. Data: normalized hash, per-message hashes, request body.</span>
        </div>
        <div class="assertion">
          <span class="assertion-type">model.response</span>
          <span class="assertion-desc">Model API response. Data: response body including tool calls.</span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="prose" style="margin-top: var(--space-lg);">
        <p>Tool calls and tool results are embedded inside <code>model.request</code> and <code>model.response</code> bodies. They are not separate event types.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Hash matching -->
  <section>
    <div class="container container--narrow">
      <h2 id="matching">Request matching</h2>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>During replay, incoming requests are matched to recorded requests by normalized SHA-256 hash of the message content. This is the most important design decision in the format.</p>
        <p>Matching by hash instead of sequence number means that minor upstream changes (prompt preamble, system message formatting) don&rsquo;t break replay as long as the substantive message content is unchanged.</p>
        <p>Each request includes both a <code>normalizedHash</code> (hash of the full normalized request) and per-message hashes in <code>messageHashes</code> for divergence localization.</p>
      </div>

      <h3 style="margin-top: var(--space-xl);">Replay modes</h3>
      <div class="assertion-list" style="margin-top: var(--space-md);">
        <div class="assertion">
          <span class="assertion-type">strict</span>
          <span class="assertion-desc">Hash miss aborts replay and reports which message diverged.</span>
        </div>
        <div class="assertion">
          <span class="assertion-type">lenient</span>
          <span class="assertion-desc">Hash miss falls back to positional matching with warnings.</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Blob storage -->
  <section>
    <div class="container container--narrow">
      <h2 id="blobs">Blob storage</h2>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>Large payloads are stored as content-addressed files in the <code>blobs/</code> directory. Trace events reference them with <code>blob:sha256-...</code> URIs.</p>
        <p>This keeps <code>trace.json</code> small and readable while preserving the full payload for replay.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Meta -->
  <section>
    <div class="container container--narrow">
      <h2 id="meta">meta.json</h2>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>Contains recording metadata: timestamp, agent command, environment information, and repro version. Secrets are redacted at capture time.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Assertions -->
  <section>
    <div class="container container--narrow">
      <h2 id="assertions">assertions.json</h2>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>Optional file containing assertions to check during replay.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="assertion-list" style="margin-top: var(--space-md);">
        {ASSERTION_TYPES.map(a => (
          <div class="assertion">
            <span class="assertion-type">{a.type}</span>
            <span class="assertion-desc">{a.desc}</span>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- REPRO.md -->
  <section>
    <div class="container container--narrow">
      <h2 id="manifest">REPRO.md manifest</h2>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>The manifest lists all known agent failures in the project. It is a Markdown file readable without installing anything.</p>
      </div>
      <CodeBlock filename="REPRO.md" id="spec-repro-md" code={REPRO_MD_CONTENT} />
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Secret redaction -->
  <section>
    <div class="container container--narrow">
      <h2 id="redaction">Secret redaction</h2>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>Secrets are redacted at capture time, before any data touches disk. The proxy detects and removes:</p>
        <ul style="margin-top: var(--space-sm); padding-left: 1.5em; list-style: disc;">
          <li>Environment variables containing keys or tokens</li>
          <li>API keys (Anthropic, OpenAI, and common patterns)</li>
          <li>JWTs</li>
          <li>PEM blocks</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

</Base>
